'll choose **P: a2-a4**. This move directly challenges Black's premature b5 advance. If Black captures axb5, I open the a-file and can potentially exploit the weakened queenside. If Black doesn't capture, the b5 pawn becomes even more of a target. This move punishes Black's unusual second move and creates immediate tactical problems for my opponent. It's more forcing than the solid developing moves and takes advantage of Black's positional mistake.\n\nAnswer: P: a2-a4"}
