ote to a queen via a8 (capturing the rook) or c8 (capturing the bishop). Capturing on c8 removes a defensive piece and places my new queen more centrally, closer to Black's exposed king.\n\nReason: Promoting the pawn to a queen by capturing the bishop on c8 gives me overwhelming material advantage (I'll have two queens) and places the new queen actively in Black's position near their exposed king on f8. This should lead to a quick checkmate. The immediate promotion is far superior to any other move.\n\nAnswer: P: b7-c8-q"}
