 less forcing than the checking moves.\n\nReason: **Q: c8-g8+** is the strongest move because:\n- It gives check, forcing Black's response\n- After the King moves (Kh6, Kf6, or Kf7 are the only legal moves), I can capture the Rook on h8 with Qxh8\n- This wins a full Rook (worth ~5 points of material)\n- Combined with my existing Queen advantage, this should lead to an easy endgame win\n- It's a forcing move that doesn't allow Black any counterplay\n\nAnswer: Q: c8-g8"}
