n c5, the resulting position should be manageable for White.\n\nReason: Trading queens with Q: e5-e3 removes Black's main attacking weapon while my pieces remain well-coordinated. Given that Black's king is more exposed on c5 than mine on e1, the endgame/simplified position should favor White. This is superior to passive king moves or blocking with minor pieces that don't fundamentally solve the tactical pressure.\n\nAnswer: Q: e5-e3"}
