his seems less effective as the bishop moves to the rim.\n\n6. **N: b1-c3** - Develops the knight toward the center, preparing to increase pressure.\n\nReason: I'll play **P: d2-d4** to establish central control, open potential lines for my pieces, and prepare to develop my remaining pieces with tempo. This move strengthens my center, prepares to develop my dark-squared bishop, and gives me better control of the board. It's a fundamental chess principle to control the center, and this move does exactly that while keeping flexibility in my position.\n\nAnswer: P: d2-d4"}
