**\nB: c4-f7 delivers check to the Black king on e7, forcing Black into a defensive response. This is a forcing move that seizes the initiative. After Bf7+, the Black king must move (likely Kd8, Kd6, Ke8, or Kf8), and I maintain pressure while keeping my active bishop well-placed. Checks and forcing moves should be examined first, and this one appears sound - the bishop is safe on f7 and disrupts Black's coordination.\n\n**Answer:** B: c4-f7"}
