s **N: f7-h8**, which gives check. After the king moves (likely Kg8, Kf8, or Kh6), I can reposition my knight or continue the attack. However, **B: g5-h6** is also extremely strong as it puts immediate pressure on the king and controls critical dark squares around it.\n\nReason: Between N: f7-h8 (check) and B: g5-h6 (attacking king), the bishop move seems more powerful because:\n- It directly threatens the king on g7\n- It controls escape squares\n- The knight check on h8 allows Kg8 or Kf8, and then the knight is somewhat out of play on h8\n- B: g5-h6 maintains persistent pressure and better piece coordination\n\nAnswer: B: g5-h6"}
