eck from the 8th rank, forcing Black's king to move (likely Kd8, Ke7, or Kf7). This check:\n- Forces Black to react defensively\n- Maintains my rook's dominance on the back rank\n- Keeps maximum pressure on Black's position\n- May lead to further tactical opportunities after the king moves\n\nThis forcing move maintains White's advantage and keeps Black under constant pressure.\n\nAnswer: R: a7-a8"}
