ting attack.\n\nReason: R: d7-d8 places my rook on the absolute back rank, maximizing pressure on Black's position. This move:\n- Dominates the 8th rank\n- Severely restricts Black king's mobility\n- Prepares potential mating threats with bishop coordination\n- Maintains my winning advantage with superior piece activity\n\nAnswer: R: d7-d8"}
